{"id":"spatial-self-attention-block","t":"Spatial self-attention block for feature maps","tags":["U-Net","Attention"],"d":"Medium","rt":"numpy","fn":"attn_block","tol":[1e-06,1e-08],"pkgs":[],"st":"Convolutions only see a neighbourhood. At the low-resolution levels of a diffusion U-Net, a self-attention block lets every pixel look at every other pixel, so distant parts of an image stay consistent. Each spatial position becomes a token whose features are its $C$ channels.\n\n1. Normalise: $h = \\mathrm{GN}(x)$, GroupNorm with `groups` contiguous channel groups, statistics over (group channels, $H$, $W$), population variance, $\\epsilon = 10^{-5}$, no affine.\n2. Flatten to tokens: $(B, C, H, W) \\to (B, N, C)$ with $N = HW$, token $n = y \\cdot W + x$ (row-major over pixels).\n3. Single-head attention with row-vector weights: $Q = hW_q$, $K = hW_k$, $V = hW_v$, then\n$$A = \\mathrm{softmax}\\!\\left(\\frac{QK^\\top}{\\sqrt{C}}\\right), \\qquad O = (AV)\\,W_o$$\nwith the softmax over keys (the last axis).\n4. Reshape $O$ back to $(B, C, H, W)$ and return $x + O$.\n\nWrite `attn_block(x, Wq, Wk, Wv, Wo, groups)`.\n\n## Inputs\n- `x`: `(B, C, H, W)` float array.\n- `Wq`, `Wk`, `Wv`, `Wo`: `(C, C)`, applied as `tokens @ W`.\n- `groups`: positive integer dividing $C$.\n\n## Output\n`(B, C, H, W)` float array. Use a numerically stable softmax (subtract the row max).","starter":"import numpy as np\n\ndef attn_block(x, Wq, Wk, Wv, Wo, groups):\n    \"\"\"x: (B, C, H, W). Return x + self-attention over the H*W positions, same shape.\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError\n","hints":["Pixels are the tokens and channels are the features. `h.reshape(B, C, H*W).transpose(0, 2, 1)` gives `(B, N, C)` in row-major pixel order.","With tokens in rows, every projection is a right-multiplication `tok @ W`, and the score matrix is `q @ k.transpose(0, 2, 1) / sqrt(C)`, shape `(B, N, N)`.","After `(a @ v) @ Wo`, undo the flattening with `.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(B, C, H, W)`. Transposing first matters: reshaping `(B, N, C)` straight to `(B, C, H, W)` scrambles channels and pixels."],"sol":"import numpy as np\n\ndef group_norm(h, groups, eps=1e-5):\n    B, C, H, W = h.shape\n    g = h.reshape(B, groups, C // groups, H, W)\n    g = (g - g.mean(axis=(2, 3, 4), keepdims=True)) / np.sqrt(g.var(axis=(2, 3, 4), keepdims=True) + eps)\n    return g.reshape(B, C, H, W)\n\ndef attn_block(x, Wq, Wk, Wv, Wo, groups):\n    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n    B, C, H, W = x.shape\n    tok = group_norm(x, groups).reshape(B, C, H * W).transpose(0, 2, 1)   # (B, N, C), row-major pixels\n    q, k, v = tok @ Wq, tok @ Wk, tok @ Wv\n    s = q @ k.transpose(0, 2, 1) / np.sqrt(C)                             # (B, N, N)\n    a = np.exp(s - s.max(axis=-1, keepdims=True))\n    a /= a.sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    o = (a @ v) @ Wo                                                      # (B, N, C)\n    return x + o.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(B, C, H, W)\n","ex_md":"## Why it works\nAfter flattening, this is ordinary self-attention over $N = HW$ tokens. Each output pixel is a convex combination of all value vectors, weighted by query-key similarity, so information moves across the whole image in one layer. The residual connection plus a zero-initialised $W_o$ (test 1) makes the block start as the identity.\n\nWith zero query and key weights (test 2) every score is $0$, the softmax is uniform, and each pixel receives the mean of the normalised feature map.\n\n## Complexity\n$O(B\\,N^2\\,C + B\\,N\\,C^2)$ time and $O(B\\,N^2)$ memory for the attention matrix. That quadratic cost in pixels is why U-Nets only attend at $16\\times16$ or $8\\times8$ resolution.\n\n## Common bugs\n- Reshaping `(B, N, C)` straight to `(B, C, H, W)` without transposing back. Shapes match, values are scrambled.\n- Scaling by $\\sqrt{N}$ instead of $\\sqrt{C}$ (the key dimension).\n- Softmax over the query axis instead of the key axis.\n\n## Interview follow-ups\n- How would you add text conditioning here? (Cross-attention: queries from pixels, keys and values from text tokens.)\n- How does multi-head attention change the shapes and the cost?","tests":[{"a":[{"__nd__":[[[[1.0,0.0]],[[0.0,1.0]]]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[1.0,0.0],[0.0,1.0]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[1.0,0.0],[0.0,1.0]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[1.0,0.0],[0.0,1.0]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[0.0,0.0],[0.0,0.0]],"dtype":"float64"},1],"e":{"__nd__":[[[[1.0,0.0]],[[0.0,1.0]]]],"dtype":"float64"}},{"a":[{"__nd__":[[[[1.0,0.0]],[[0.0,1.0]]]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[0.0,0.0],[0.0,0.0]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[0.0,0.0],[0.0,0.0]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[1.0,0.0],[0.0,1.0]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[1.0,0.0],[0.0,1.0]],"dtype":"float64"},2],"e":{"__nd__":[[[[1.0,0.0]],[[0.0,1.0]]]],"dtype":"float64"}},{"a":[{"__nd__":[[[[1.101262453505847,0.3384312766461778],[-0.5399715152535035,-1.2602418568524327]],[[-1.8946212698392553,0.018638290983285614],[-0.8105670995116028,-0.8721559599345132]]]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[1.0,0.0],[0.0,1.0]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[1.0,0.0],[0.0,1.0]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[1.0,0.0],[0.0,1.0]],"dtype":"float64"},{"__nd__":[[1.0,0.0],[0.0,1.0]],"dtype":"float64"},1],"e":{"__nd__":[[[[2.804922235144234,1.235419250316005],[-0.045993998031080396,-1.3442422585900102]],[[-3.3792058726444445,-0.33358691132776674],[-1.3968821957618598,-1.3189444970977067]]]],"dtype":"float64"}},{"a":[{"__nd__":[[[[-0.22196950708389104,-0.05184602813201771],[-2.2767828157758307,0.9251465905764266],[-2.026845605910026,1.8596241085543468]],[[0.5905681115998624,-0.47184451813331413],[1.342996537380774,0.020786461917443023],[0.6909209676232841,0.10722707944720507]],[[1.096531380130275,1.0614224543758295],[-0.9073341413930657,-0.6124917784436158],[0.3432270521124315,-0.21001015163517062]],[[-2.284914216554451,2.0261175349217764],[-2.174977373868806,-2.081542853744764],[-1.2761124197329383,0.5648512404463458]]],[[[1.7960125066302708,-0.23541505259008